      "id": "internshipdeadlines",
      "project": "InternshipDeadlines",
      "title": "Opportunity instrument",
      "concept": "A dished enamel perpetual-calendar chapter carries thirty-one original serif dates fitted to its curved face inside a deep profiled barrel. A broad seated Roman bezel, fitted seven-day enamel insert and dark steel leaf hand establish a clear working face. An open three-foot movement casting reveals seated wheels beneath the register. A stepped arbor, fitted winding crowns, rear service windows and pear pendulum complete the horological instrument. Engraved case and index details inherit their mechanical parent motion.",
